# Python Code Style Rule

## Version and Formatting
- Use Python 3.10+ compatible syntax.
- Follow PEP8 strictly.
- Keep line length at 88 characters (Black baseline).

## Typing and Documentation
- Require type hints for all function parameters and return values.
- Require Google-style docstrings for all public functions, methods, and classes.

## Maintainability
- Prefer explicit names over abbreviations.
- Avoid hidden side effects in utility functions.
